# Security review 10/25: working files that are not part of the app and must
# not ride along to GitHub / the Render image. Workbooks at the repo root are
# business data (inventory with cost, prospects, pay calculators); the "-1"
# files are stale backup copies; Claude outputs/ are review artifacts.
/*.xlsx
/*.xlsm
/*.csv
# 11/12: widened from "-1" only. Saving a file from a Claude file card into a
# folder that already has that name makes "name-1.ext", then "-2", "-3" ...
# (server-4.js, scripts/epass-odbc-pull-1.ps1). They are duplicates of the
# real file and never belong on GitHub. One digit after the last hyphen, so
# names like docs/security/audit-2026-10.md are untouched.
/*-[0-9].js
/*-[0-9].html
/*-[0-9].css
/*-[0-9].md
lib/*-[0-9].js
scripts/*-[0-9].ps1
scripts/*-[0-9].js
scripts/*-[0-9].mjs
docs/**/*-[0-9].md
lib/pilot-seed.js
/Claude outputs/
service_call_journey/service_call_journey/Claude outputs/
/screenshots/
/samples/
/API Docs/
# "spec sheets" is tracked since 11/12: the Express shop links the sell sheets in it
# (data/shop-spec-sheets.json). It is still never served as a static folder.
# The nested service_call_journey/service_call_journey/ copy had slipped past
# the rules above (10/25) — cover the data folders at any depth.
service_call_journey/**/reference/data/
service_call_journey/**/reference/*.xlsx
service_call_journey/**/reference/*.zip
